{"availability":"available","full":"materialdigital/core-ontology","name":"core-ontology","description":"The PMD Core Ontology (PMDco) official release repository","category":"Other","language":"Jupyter Notebook","stars":49,"forks":20,"created":"2021-07-15T09:26:00Z","updated":"2026-10-09T16:20:37Z","license":"CC-BY-4.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://materialdigital.github.io/core-ontology/docs/","topics":[],"demo":"https://materialdigital.github.io/core-ontology/docs/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:04:38.371Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T21:04:38.371Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T21:04:38.371Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T21:04:38.371Z","stars":49,"forks":20}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Documentation · Class Reference · Patterns · Discussions · Issues","The Platform MaterialDigital Core Ontology (PMDco) is a mid-level semantic framework for Materials Science and Engineering (MSE). Aligning with the ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021 standard, PMDco is built on the Basic Formal Ontology (BFO) and reuses several BFO-aligned ontologies such as RO, IAO, and OBI. Its scope follows the fundamental paradigm of MSE — processing, structure, and properties — and provides general semantics for entities commonly required across MSE disciplines, such as devices, roles, functions, and plans.","MSE-related process chains, including materials manufacturing, characterization, and simulation processes."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/materialdigital/core-ontology/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4f1b9dde922581ad66c30cd4ef91600a6dd2820214767ec163bacefe8b4182a8","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T21:04:38.577Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:04:38.577Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Documentation · Class Reference · Patterns · Discussions · Issues","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/materialdigital/core-ontology/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerpri